FILE: vUX-resizer.js
FEATURE: component-teardown
DATE: 2026-09-17
PRIOR STATE: as left by feature 'resizer-docs'

REASON
Resizer already had a working destroy(); only the freeze convention was missing. Its
public members are now non-writable like every other component's. Note that Resizer's
destroy() guards on 'initialized' rather than a 'destroyed' flag, and so deliberately
permits initialize() again afterwards — the other components follow DataView and refuse.
That difference is intentional and left as it was.

